diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -2106,6 +2106,42 @@
 
             ``--audio-device=alsa/dmix:default``
 
+
+``--audio-pcm-content=<all|lfe|bass|lfe-bass>``
+    Select the content of the secondary decoded PCM output configured with
+    ``--audio-pcm-device`` (default: ``all``). Requires primary bitstream playback.
+
+    ``all`` preserves the decoded channel layout. ``lfe`` copies the named LFE
+    channel at its decoded level to both left and right of a stereo output,
+    suitable for a two-channel USB DAC/DSP. A track without an LFE channel sends
+    stereo silence. This does not redirect bass from the other channels or add
+    an LFE gain boost. The primary bitstream is unaffected. Summing both identical
+    channels downstream increases their combined level.
+
+    ``bass`` redirects every main channel through a fourth-order Linkwitz-Riley
+    low-pass filter and combines the result with LFE at +10 dB relative gain.
+    The identical bass signal is sent to both stereo channels. LFE retains its
+    authored bandwidth. The fixed 20.2 dB headroom rounds up the 20.14 dB
+    worst-case coherent 7.1 channel sum. Layouts larger than 7.1 reserve additional
+    headroom. This is constant attenuation, with no limiter or normalization of
+    program peaks. Calibrate the external device for this output level. The
+    summation allowance assumes nominal full-scale decoded PCM; filter/resampler
+    overshoot and downstream gain, EQ or summation are not bounded by it.
+
+    ``lfe-bass`` sends raw LFE to the left channel, as in ``lfe`` mode, and the
+    bass-managed mix to the right, as in ``bass`` mode. Only the right channel
+    uses the crossover and 20.2 dB bass headroom. Without LFE, left is silent
+    while right still carries redirected main-channel bass. Calibrate the two
+    downstream signal paths independently: the LFE component in the right
+    channel is 10.2 dB below the left.
+
+    The secondary output retains its existing delay and clock synchronization.
+    Changing content during playback reinitializes audio and refreshes playback.
+
+``--audio-pcm-crossover=<20-250>``
+    Common crossover in Hz for all main channels in secondary bass-managed PCM
+    (default: 80). LFE is not filtered by this crossover. The primary bitstream
+    and the receiver's speaker crossover settings are unaffected.
 
 ``--audio-exclusive=<yes|no>``
     Enable exclusive output mode. In this mode, the system is usually locked
